# oracle: pair_style comb3 polar_off with pair_coeff * * ffield.comb3 Cu C (C in the element list, so lib.comb3 is read) but only Cu atoms (type 1) in a 3x3x3 fcc cell, 0.05 A random displacement, all charges 0: run 0, then 5 NVE steps; per-atom forces of the final state (dump) and thermo rows. Checks the library reader and the table set-up without carbon atoms
# native: installed lmp (b332f28 build, which includes COMB3). Measured error (engine vs native): worst per-atom force relative error 7.66e-15 (atom 18 fx, after 5 steps). The 1e-8 target holds on every row.
# oracle-potentials: ffield.comb3 lib.comb3
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 atomrel=1e-8
units		metal
atom_style	charge
dimension       3
boundary        p p p
lattice  	fcc 3.615
region		box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box	2 box
create_atoms	1 box
mass		1 63.546
mass		2 12.011
displace_atoms  all random 0.05 0.05 0.05 4417 units box
pair_style	comb3 polar_off
pair_coeff	* * ffield.comb3 Cu C
neighbor	2.0 bin
neigh_modify	every 1 delay 0 check yes
fix		1 all nve
timestep        0.00020
thermo_style	custom step temp etotal pe evdwl ecoul press vol lx ly lz
thermo_modify	norm yes format float %.15g
thermo		5
run		0
run		5
